      "id": "f3bb3371-165c-4af8-abfa-fc52ded11df0",
      "name": "Sticky Note",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        0,
        0
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "width": 480,
        "height": 864,
        "content": "## Track daily stock sentiment from Twitter and Yahoo Finance to Google Drive\n\n### Who's it for\n\nTraders, analysts, and finance-curious builders who want to track daily market sentiment across social chatter and price data without paying for a closed platform.\n\n### How it works\n\nThis workflow runs every day at 9am and starts two parallel Apify data collection jobs: one for stock-related tweets and one for stock market data. Each branch aggregates the retrieved items, converts the aggregated results into a JSON file, and uploads the file to Google Drive. The canvas is organized as a trigger on the left feeding two horizontal processing lanes: tweets on top and stock data below.\n\n### Setup steps\n\n- Configure the Schedule Trigger with the correct timezone and desired 9am daily run settings.\n- Add valid Apify credentials and configure the selected actors or tasks for scraping stock tweets and fetching stock data.\n- Configure the aggregation and JSON conversion nodes so they include the fields you want saved.\n- Connect Google Drive credentials and set the destination folder and file naming rules for both uploads.\n\n### Customization\n\nAdjust the Apify actor inputs to change target tickers, search terms, date ranges, or data sources, and update the Google Drive file names or folders to match your reporting structure."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "975df785-fd09-47a0-9142-148bc155dacc",
